{"url": "https://ece.engin.umich.edu/", "final_url": "https://ece.engin.umich.edu/", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-01", "text": "Giving\n|\nAlumni\nAbout\nAcademics\nResearch\nPeople\nCommunity\nNews\nEvents\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nPeople Powering Innovation\nElectrical and Computer Engineering (ECE)\nElectrical and Computer Engineering is the technological foundation of modern society, and the unseen force behind today\u2019s intelligent systems. With its impact on clean energy, precision health, cybersecurity, autonomy, communications, the quantum revolution and more, ECE holds the key to a better society.\nAs one of the most respected programs in the world, Electrical and Computer Engineering at the University of Michigan provides a progressive curriculum, internationally-recognized faculty, and an intellectual community that values diversity, interdisciplinary teamwork, entrepreneurial thinking, and inventiveness. Our areas of impact include:\nsmart electronics\nenergy and power\ninformation\ncommunication\nautomation + robotics\nGraduate Programs\nGrad programs and Admissions in Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) >\nPhD Program>\nMaster of Science (MS/MSE) Program >\nMaster of Engineering (MEng) Program>\nApply Now >\nUndergraduate Programs\nElectrical Engineering Major >\nComputer Engineering Major >\nElectrical Engineering Minor >\nComputer Engineering Minor >\nUndergraduate Advising Office >\nApply Now >\nECE Research\nElectrical and Computer Engineering at Michigan is a top-ranked, world-class department that is pushing the boundaries of research in the most high-tech and innovative areas affecting society.\nExplore Research in ECE >\nResearch Areas >\nQuick Links\nMake an undergraduate advising appointment >\nGrad School Admissions Requirements >\nProspective Graduate Students >\nCourse Information >\nGraduate Course List by Area >\nECE BY THE NUMBERS\n$52.4M\nIn Research\nExpenditures\n1,537\nRemarkable\nStudents\nTop 10\nUG and Grad\nPrograms\n93\nAward-Winning\nFaculty\nThe Magic of ECE\nDiscover the world of electrical and computer engineering, where you can impact people\u2019s lives for the better\nEvents\nOCT\n30\nSTUDENT EVENT\nHalloween Party\n11:00am \u2013 1:00pm in EECS Atrium\nOCT\n30\nCONTROL SEMINAR\nSpacecraft Computationally-Aware, Real-Time Optimizations for Guidance and Control\n3:30pm \u2013 4:30pm in 1500 EECS Building\nNOV\n03\nSTUDENT EVENT\nEngineer Your Future: 2026 ECE Graduate Program Virtual Information Session (International Student Information)\n8:30am \u2013 9:30am in Virtual\nNOV\n03\nSTUDENT EVENT\nPanel Workshop \u2013 Navigating the ECE Faculty Job Market\n1:00pm \u2013 2:30pm in 3316 EECS\nAll ECE Events >\nNews\nBeyond transistor limits: Hybrid magnetic-sound waves could boost computing speed and efficiency\nAn alternative to the transistor, made with multiferroic materials, could make computers up to 1,000 times faster and more energy-efficient.\nAdil Dogan joins inaugural cohort of James Lu World Fellows\nDogan joins three other students receiving the award, which supports global doctoral scholars pursuing groundbreaking work in engineering fields.\nCindy Finelli receives IEEE William E. Sayle II Award for Achievement in Education\nProfessor Finelli is recognized for her leadership in engineering education research and integrating ethics into engineering curricula.\nAll ECE News >\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nEECS Building\n1301 Beal Avenue\nAnn Arbor, MI 48109-2122\nDidn't find what you were looking for? Contact Us\nFaculty and Staff Resources: ECE Intranet\nElectrical and Computer Engineering is one of two divisions in the Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science. The other is Computer Science and Engineering. We are part of the College of Engineering at the University of Michigan.\n\u00a9 2026 The Regents of the University of Michigan\nPrivacy Policy\nCampus Safety\nNon-Discrimination Policy\nAbout\nAca